{"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"],"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","generated":true}],"abstract":[{"text":"Implement registration, cloning, snapshots and inspection for a component from its stored properties.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Generating components with the component macro"},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/componentmacro"]}],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FirebladeECSMacros"},{"type":"text","text":" product provides the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Component"},{"type":"text","text":" macro."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It turns a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"struct"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"enum"},{"type":"text","text":" into a component and implements a set of component protocols from its stored properties, so you don’t have to write that code by hand:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Protocol","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Generated"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Enables"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/RegistrableComponent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"stable "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"componentTypeName"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nexus.register(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nexus.registeredComponentTypes"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nexus.componentType(named:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/CloneableComponent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(cloning:context:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clone(context:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"entity.clone()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"nexus.clone(entities:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"nexus.clone(into:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SerializableComponent","type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CodingKeys"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode(to:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"nexus.encodeSnapshot(using:handling:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"nexus.restoreSnapshot(from:using:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"nexus.decodeSnapshot(from:using:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Nexus: Codable","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/InspectableComponent","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"componentProperties"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"generic inspection, e.g. in editors"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/DefaultInitializable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init()"},{"type":"text","text":" if every stored property has a default value (structs)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"key path assignment, state machines"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Component","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"static let componentIndex","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"typed lookups read a plain static instead of taking the registry lock","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The core "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FirebladeECS"},{"type":"text","text":" library stays dependency free. Only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FirebladeECSMacros"},{"type":"text","text":" depends on "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-syntax","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"All protocols can also be implemented by hand without the macro."}]},{"text":"Adding the product","level":3,"anchor":"Adding-the-product","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the product to your target. It does not re-export "},{"code":"FirebladeECS","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": add the ","type":"text"},{"code":"FirebladeECS","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" product too and import both modules in every file that uses ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Component","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":[".target(","    name: \"YourTargetName\",","    dependencies: [","        .product(name: \"FirebladeECS\", package: \"ecs\"),","        .product(name: \"FirebladeECSMacros\", package: \"ecs\")","    ])"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Declaring components","level":3,"anchor":"Declaring-components","type":"heading"},{"code":["import FirebladeECS","import FirebladeECSMacros","","@Component","struct Transform {","    var position: SIMD3<Float> = .zero","    var parent: EntityIdentifier?","    @ComponentIgnored var cachedMatrix: [Float] = []  \/\/ still cloned, but not serialized or inspected","}","","@Component(excluding: .serializable)  \/\/ runtime-only component","struct RenderHandle: @unchecked Sendable {","    var handle: Int = 0","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The stable type name defaults to the fully qualified type name. Declare ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static let componentTypeName"},{"text":" to override it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After renaming a persisted type, list its former names in "},{"code":"static let componentTypeNameAliases","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so existing snapshots keep loading. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Component(excluding:)"},{"text":" takes a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ComponentMacroFeatures"},{"text":" set: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cloneable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".serializable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".inspectable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".defaultInit"},{"type":"text","text":". Registration is always implemented."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@ComponentIgnored"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps a stored property out of serialization and inspection. Ignored properties are still cloned and need a default value."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Serialized properties need an explicit type annotation. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"let"},{"type":"text","text":" constants with an initial value are not serialized."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Members you declare yourself are not generated. Declaring any of ","type":"text"},{"code":"CodingKeys","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"encode(to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves serialization entirely to you.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The generated initializers live in an extension, so a struct keeps its memberwise initializer. A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"public"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"package"},{"text":" struct, and a struct that declares initializers, gets a generated ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init()"},{"text":" in its body (the implicit ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init()"},{"text":" is internal and disappears next to declared initializers); an internal struct without initializers keeps the implicit one.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An enum is cloned as a whole and listed without properties. It is serialized only if it declares ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" itself, and it gets ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DefaultInitializable"},{"text":" only if it declares ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The macro stores ","type":"text"},{"code":"static let componentIndex = registeredComponentIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The index still comes from the registry at first access, so it cannot collide with a lazily assigned one. Declare your own ","type":"text"},{"code":"componentIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to opt out.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Value types and diagnostics","anchor":"Value-types-and-diagnostics"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Component","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reports an error when it is applied to a class: components are value types, so use a struct or enum. The nexus also asserts once per component type, in debug builds, that a hand-written conformance is not a class.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A stored property spelled ","type":"text"},{"code":"Entity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Entity?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Entity]"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Set<Entity>"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Key: Entity]"},{"text":" is an error with a fix-it that replaces ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Entity"},{"text":" by ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/EntityIdentifier","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". An ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" keeps its nexus alive and is not valid after a copy, a clone or a snapshot, while an identifier is a plain value that the clone context remaps. The macro sees syntax only: an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Entity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" behind a typealias or in a nested type is not diagnosed and stays a convention."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Registering, cloning and snapshots","anchor":"Registering-cloning-and-snapshots","type":"heading","level":3},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let nexus = Nexus()","try nexus.register([Transform.self, RenderHandle.self])","","\/\/ Clone a whole world; entity references (`parent`) are remapped to the clones.","let playMode = Nexus()","try nexus.clone(into: playMode)","","\/\/ Export and import all serializable components, keyed by their stable type names.","var encoder = JSONEncoder()","let data = try nexus.encodeSnapshot(using: &encoder, handling: .skip)","var decoder = JSONDecoder()","try playMode.decodeSnapshot(from: data, using: &decoder)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Component types are registered automatically the first time an instance is assigned."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Register them explicitly before decoding snapshots that reference them.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusSnapshot","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" starts with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"formatVersion"},{"type":"text","text":" and keeps the original entity identifiers."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Decoding creates new entities, remaps entity references to them through an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/EntityReferenceResolver","isActive":true},{"text":", and rejects snapshots written in a newer format version.","type":"text"}]}]}],"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/InspectableComponent":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"InspectableComponent"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A component that describes its stored properties for generic inspection, e.g. by editors or diff tools."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/inspectablecomponent","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/InspectableComponent","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"InspectableComponent"}],"title":"InspectableComponent","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ChoosingAStorage":{"title":"Choosing a storage","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage","role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the sparse-set or the archetype storage for a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and know what changes."}],"kind":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEvent":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A marker protocol for all Nexus events."}],"title":"NexusEvent","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NexusEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexusevent","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NexusEvent","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/Storage